mod:param_redef_store_prices;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 2: DEF-685, seat D2's D5, stacked on row 1). A STORE THROUGH A POINTER PARAMETER THE CALLEE REDEFINED LANDS
// WHERE THE PARAMETER NOW POINTS, not in the argument first passed (`a = b; (<-a).lp = v`). The escape analysis walks a MARKED parameter's own
// chain (where the body pointed it) BESIDE main's record of the store at the parameter, never in its place, so the callee's summary records the
// store and the caller's view across the call is refused. A parameter is marked only on three roads: (1) it is assigned whole (`a = b`, in one
// branch too); (2) refs land on its own address ref (`rp = @r; <-rp = p2`); (3) `@o` or `$$ o`, under casts too, is handed to a callee whose
// summary stores refs through that parameter (`bothp(@o, o, p2, hq)`). An address taken alone (`rdhp(@p)`) marks nothing.
// THE PRICES (8), AT PARITY on DEF-685's line: `e_slvp_ok`, `e_slvp_un`, `p_backm`, `p_backm2`, `a4_pvaa`, `a4_pvaa_ok`, `a4_pw`, `a4_pw_ok`.
// Each runs 67 on main (acb78ea) and on row 1, and is refused here, because a redefined parameter now gets main's own treatment of a redefined
// local. Each sits beside its local-copy twin, the same program with the parameter copied into a local first, which main refuses at the same site
// (TWINS, 8: `e_slvp_lc`, `e_slvp_br2`, `p_backlc2`, `a4_pvlc`, `a4_pvlc_ok`, `a4_pwlc`, `a4_pwlc_ok`, `t_pcalf_lc_ok`). `t_pcalf_lc_ok` is the
// twin of row 1's `t_pcalf_ok`, whose added site this row puts in unwrap_param_store_prices.npk. No price here is off parity, so the row takes no
// new number.
error:E5;
